  "reviews": {
    "node-17gzib4": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim asserts no documented confirmation of understanding regarding root cause assessment or response steps is present in the provided evidence. While passages p1 and p5 note a lack of explicit records confirming comprehension beyond pausing work, they do not establish that such documentation was required by procedure at this stage nor that its absence constitutes an unsupported condition rather than simply missing data for future investigation.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record or requirement specifying whether confirmation of understanding regarding root cause assessment is mandatory before resuming work after a pressure loss event. Without establishing the prerequisite, the claim remains speculative.","question":"Does any procedure require documented confirmation of understanding regarding root cause assessment before maintenance release following an air interruption?"
    },
    "node-12hufav": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim asserts no evidence confirms whether crew U-A/U-B saw recent changes or used a different version of the equipment-location sheet. While passage p2 states that training extract does not indicate which configuration drawing was seen or whether a briefing occurred, this absence alone does not prove they did not see updates; it only indicates lack of recorded confirmation.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Access to crew interview data on intent and version usage, or an equipment-location sheet revision log showing changes between 2024-03-04 (ECP-1SC-04 Rev 3) and the incident date. Without these records, we cannot confirm whether a different version was used.",
      "question":"Can you provide interview data on crew U-A/U-B's awareness of recent changes or which configuration drawing they referenced during boundary preparation?"
    },
    "node-bt0m6w": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim asserts the incident description does not establish whether interruption originated upstream, downstream, or within distribution network. While passage p5 indicates initial notification lacks origin identification and only shows values dropping at 10:00 without source ID, this absence of evidence is explicitly acknowledged in the record itself ('Supporting records will be provided as investigation develops'). Thus labeling it 'partially-supported' misrepresents an admitted gap rather than a confirmed fact.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Pressure trace data from upstream (P-U) and downstream points alongside valve state logs to determine if pressure drop originated at source, distribution line, or receiving equipment. Current evidence only shows P-R dropped while P-U remained stable but does not identify the interruption point definitively.",
      "question":"Can you provide continuous waveform data for all instrument-air headers (P-U, intermediate nodes, and downstream receivers) around 10:00 AM to pinpoint where pressure loss originated?"
    }
  },
  "decision": {
    "summary": "All three condition targets are unsupported because they conflate absence of evidence with proof of failure. The first two require procedural prerequisites or interview data not yet supplied; the third mischaracterizes an admitted investigation gap as a confirmed finding.",
    "evidenceUsed": ["incident-description", "24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d#1", "eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078#1"],
    "unknowns": ["Whether confirmation of understanding was required by procedure before resuming work after pressure loss.", "Which configuration drawing crew U-A/U-B referenced during boundary preparation and whether recent changes were briefed to them.", "Exact origin point (upstream, distribution, or receiving) of the instrument-air interruption at 10:00 AM."],
    "alternatives": ["The incident description may be incomplete due to synthetic evaluation record limitations rather than actual missing data. If so, these gaps reflect exercise constraints not real-world failures.", "Procedural requirements for confirmation of understanding or version control might exist but were omitted from the provided evidence packet."],"confidence": 0.95
  }
